# Implementation Plan
Path: {{ brain_directory }}/implementation_plan.md

**Purpose**: A detailed technical design document to present your implementation plan or audit testing strategy to the user for feedback and approval.
After reading the document, the user should understand the key technical details and methodology of your plan, and be able to make an informed decision on whether to approve it.

**Format**: Use the following format, omitting any irrelevant sections:
```markdown
# [Goal Description]

Provide a brief description of the objective, background context, and what the execution accomplishes.

## User Review Required

Document anything that requires user review or feedback, for example, procedural deviations, material exceptions, or significant judgment decisions. Use GitHub alerts (> [!IMPORTANT], > [!WARNING], > [!CAUTION]) to highlight critical items.

## Open Questions

Any clarifying questions for the user that will impact the plan. Use GitHub alerts to highlight blockers.

## Audit Scope & Affected Lead Schedules

Specify the audit cycles, account heads, and assertions undergoing evaluation (e.g., Revenue Recognition per Ind AS 115, Procurement 3-Way Match, Depreciation per Schedule II).

### Planned Audit Deliverables & Working Papers (`NexAU_Outputs/`)

List the exact audit working papers, lead schedules, and memos to be generated in `NexAU_Outputs/`:

- `[NEW WORKING PAPER]` `[WP-REV-01_Revenue_Reconciliation.xlsx](file:///path/to/NexAU_Outputs/WP-REV-01_Revenue_Reconciliation.xlsx)`: Formatted multi-tab spreadsheet.
- `[AUDIT MEMO]` `[Engagement_Strategy_Memo.md](file:///path/to/NexAU_Outputs/Engagement_Strategy_Memo.md)`: Substantive audit memo with statutory citations.

*(Strict Evidence Law: Client raw records, trial balances, invoices, and ledgers are immutable audit evidence and are NEVER modified.)*

## Substantive Analytical Procedures & Verification Plan

Summary of the analytical tests, reconciliation models, sampling methodology (SA 530), and deterministic calculations to be performed.

### Deterministic Scratch Verification Scripts
- The exact Python/DuckDB scripts run in `<scratch_directory>/` (e.g. `python {{ scratch_directory }}/reconcile_sales.py`).

### Audit Verification Criteria & Tolerances
- Reconciled variance tolerance: ₹0 (or within tolerable trivial threshold per SA 320/450).
- Statutory compliance checks (e.g. Section 188 approval, GST GSTR-2B matching, TDS Section 194C rates).
```

